## For agents that fetch URLs

- Country answers: https://api.voidly.ai/v1/answers/country/{CC} (plain text; add ?format=json for JSON), for example https://api.voidly.ai/v1/answers/country/IR. Each gives the censorship index score with its data time, the latest citable incidents with readable IDs and links, and what it does not know: per-domain checks were paused (HTTP 503 ACCESSIBILITY_REVIEW_HOLD) when read on 2026-10-19, and no forecast is included. Answers are cached for up to five minutes. Overview: https://api.voidly.ai/v1/answers
- MCP Server Cards (SEP-2127): https://api.voidly.ai/mcp/server-card, https://api.voidly.ai/mcp/voidpay/server-card, https://api.voidly.ai/mcp/mail/server-card. A card gives the server name, version, transport and protocol versions; it lists no tools. AI Catalog: https://api.voidly.ai/.well-known/ai-catalog.json and https://voidly.ai/.well-known/ai-catalog.json.
- One-click install links for Cursor, VS Code and Claude, and the Claude Code command: https://voidly.ai/agents#connect
- Agent skill: `npx skills add voidly-ai/atlas-mcp --skill check-censorship` (https://github.com/voidly-ai/atlas-mcp/tree/main/skills/check-censorship). It uses only no-auth reads and states its limits.

## Historical voidpay session safety — August 2026

Historical session-rail notes from August 2026 follow. Their entry points, availability observations and settlement counts describe those dated tests, not the current marketplace. This is a dated record, not a current checkout guide. Use the marketplace links above for current product entry points.

Every https://api.voidly.ai/v1/pay/* route other than the four session POSTs (/v1/pay/session/redeem, /deliver, /recover, /reattest) answers HTTP 410 PAY_RUNTIME_WITHHELD to public callers, a further exception being Voidly's own version-pinned release canary. Re-measured 2026-08-27: a GET to each of the four answers 410, a POST answers 400 or 422 — this is a dated availability observation, not current integration guidance. Those four were the documented carve-outs at that time; this record does not establish their current state. The original August 2026 caution is retained verbatim: “Those four are the only routes carved out of the containment wall, and they are being brought up under security review — do not infer their current state from this document; call them.” This quotation records the earlier warning; use current product documentation before integrating. Transfers, escrow, the credit ledger and the capability marketplace are not callable on that host.

The August 2026 Sessions records are archived evidence at https://voidly.ai/pay/verify. They describe first-party mechanism tests, not current x402 terms, customer demand, revenue, or traction.

Earlier versions described Voidpay as a zero-value test rail. That description is outdated; use the live x402 marketplace entry points above. The August Sessions notes here remain dated evidence.

No credit exists that is money, backed, redeemable, or convertible. The historical session and credit rails offer no deposits, withdrawals, bridges, on-ramps or off-ramps. **Do not send funds to any Voidly address expecting credits, backing, a balance, a refund or a return.** No transfer creates credits. The separate x402 resources advertise per-call USDC terms; see the current guide above.

- Overview: https://voidly.ai/voidly-pay.md
- Product page: https://voidly.ai/pay
- Machine-readable card: https://voidly.ai/.well-known/voidly-pay.json

